---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About Me"
  description="Learn more about me, my experience, education, and publications."
  pubDate={new Date('Jan 29 2025')}
>
  <div class="about-page">
  <section class="summary">
    <h2>Why I build AI products</h2>
    <p>
      I’m a Rome-based MLOps engineer who thrives at the intersection of applied research and production systems. I get
      teams shipping faster by pairing robust infrastructure with pragmatic workflows—from GPU orchestration and data
      pipelines to safety tooling for customer-facing agents.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="timeline">
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <div class="timeline-grid">
      <article>
        <header>
          <h3>Stip AI · Lead ML Engineer</h3>
          <p>Sep 2024 – Present · Rome, Italy</p>
        </header>
        <ul>
          <li>Built the AI organisation from the ground up, owning hiring, roadmap definition, and delivery.</li>
          <li>Designed a multi-agent voice platform on LangGraph + LangChain with tight latency budgets.</li>
          <li>Scaled RAG pipelines through metadata-rich ingestion, automated evaluation, and CI/CD.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <header>
          <h3>Translated · MLOps Engineer & AI Production Lead</h3>
          <p>Feb 2022 – Sep 2024 · Rome, Italy</p>
        </header>
        <ul>
          <li>Led a cross-functional engineering pod maintaining 100+ machine translation models in production.</li>
          <li>Migrated AI infrastructure to a geo-distributed Kubernetes + SLURM stack, reducing idle GPU time by 30%.</li>
          <li>Developed an internal annotation platform producing 100k+ high-quality datapoints for proprietary LLMs.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <header>
          <h3>Stip · AI Specialist</h3>
          <p>Sep 2021 – Feb 2022 · Rome, Italy</p>
        </header>
        <ul>
          <li>Shipped customer-care NLP solutions end-to-end—from data preparation to monitoring in production.</li>
          <li>Implemented reproducible ML workflows with MLflow, DVC, and automated deployment tooling.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <header>
          <h3>University of Rome “Tor Vergata” · NLP Research Scholar</h3>
          <p>Sep 2020 – Feb 2021 · Rome, Italy</p>
        </header>
        <ul>
          <li>Explored rule injection for neural dialog systems and authored an LREC 2022 publication.</li>
          <li>Collaborated with AlmaWave to evaluate explainability techniques for healthcare diagnostics.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="education">
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <div class="education-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>M.Sc. Computer Science · 110/110 cum laude</h3>
        <p>University of Rome “Tor Vergata” · 2019 – 2021</p>
        <p>Thesis: <em>Evaluation of Explainability of Machine Learning Models: ERO-MD Explainable Model for Migraine Diagnosis</em></p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>B.Sc. Computer Science</h3>
        <p>University of Rome “Tor Vergata” · 2016 – 2019</p>
        <p>Thesis: <em>Automation in semantic annotations and ontology population for United Nations resolutions</em></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="skills">
    <h2>Skills snapshot</h2>
    <div class="chip-grid">
      <span>Python</span>
      <span>PyTorch</span>
      <span>LangChain</span>
      <span>LangGraph</span>
      <span>TensorRT</span>
      <span>vLLM</span>
      <span>Kubernetes</span>
      <span>Docker</span>
      <span>SLURM</span>
      <span>MLflow</span>
      <span>Airflow</span>
      <span>GitHub Actions</span>
      <span>Postgres</span>
      <span>MongoDB</span>
      <span>Redis</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="recognition">
    <h2>Recognition & community</h2>
    <div class="recognition-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>EVALITA 2020 · Best System Award</h3>
        <p>1st place in the SardiStance task at the national Italian NLP competition.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Pi Campus HackParty W21 · 2nd Place</h3>
        <p>Runner-up in the AI Challenge, delivering a production-ready prototype in under 48 hours.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Student Representative & Hackathon Organizer</h3>
        <p>Advocated for Computer Science students and curated innovation events at Tor Vergata (2017–2021).</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="publications">
    <h2>Publications</h2>
    <div class="publication-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>Every Time I Fire a Conversational Designer...</h3>
        <p>LREC · 2022</p>
        <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2022.lrec-1.15.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the paper ↗</a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Combining Transformer-based Architectures for Stance Detection</h3>
        <p>EVALITA · 2020</p>
        <a href="https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2765/paper99.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the paper ↗</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="details">
    <div>
      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>DeepLearning.AI · Introduction to Machine Learning in Production (2021)</li>
        <li>Udemy · Docker and Kubernetes: The Complete Guide (2021)</li>
        <li>HackerRank · REST API (Intermediate) (2020)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Languages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Italian · Native</li>
        <li>English · B2</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  </div>

  <style>
    .about-page {
      display: grid;
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .about-page section {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .about-page .timeline-grid article header h3 {
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .about-page {
        gap: 2.25rem;
      }

      .about-page section {
        gap: 1.25rem;
      }
    }
  </style>

</Layout>
